<section class="detail-section" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" id="g31m-features" aria-labelledby="g31m-tab-features">
<article class="story"><h2>1,280Wh for the 12V loads that make an RV stop feel settled.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>100Ah rated capacity, 1,280Wh rated energy and a 100A maximum continuous-discharge rating support a planned 12V auxiliary system, not engine starting. Use the runtime guide in the gallery as an estimate, then size the inverter, fusing and wiring around your actual loads.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-final-feature-lifestyle-v2-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="SuntNeew Group 31 battery installed in an RV service bay at a lakeside campsite" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
<article class="story"><h2>Start with the tray, hold-down and cable path—not the label alone.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>The 339 × 185 × 218mm case sets the starting point for an RV auxiliary system. Confirm tray size, hold-down clearance, terminal access and cable routing before ordering; the Group 31 name does not guarantee a universal drop-in fit.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-final-feature-install-v2-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="SuntNeew Group 31 battery secured in an RV auxiliary battery bay" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
<article class="story"><h2>Bluetooth status visibility from inside the RV.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>Use compatible Bluetooth 5.0 monitoring to review state of charge, voltage, current and battery temperature before changing loads or charging sources. Follow the product manual and app instructions for the available functions.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-final-feature-bluetooth-v2-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Phone displaying Bluetooth battery status above a SuntNeew Group 31 battery in an RV" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
<article class="story"><h2>21.16 lb makes installation—and the next service visit—easier.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>At a listed 9.6kg / 21.16lb, the G31 is easier to move into service position than many comparably sized lead-acid batteries. Use the integrated carry strap for handling, then secure the case with a correctly sized tray and hold-down.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-final-feature-lightweight-v2-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="SuntNeew Group 31 LiFePO4 battery being carried beside a conventional lead-acid battery" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
<article class="story"><h2>BMS and IP65 define the battery boundary; system design completes it.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>The built-in BMS covers the listed current, voltage, temperature and short-circuit protections. IP65 means dust-tight and protected against water jets, not immersion; secure the battery upright and use correctly sized fuses, cables and terminal covers.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-amazon-aplus-bms-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Six built-in BMS protection functions for the SuntNeew Group 31 battery" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
<article class="story"><h2>Low-temperature charge protection knows when to stop and resume.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>Charging stops below 0°C battery temperature and resumes above 5°C. The listed operating ranges are 0–55°C for charging and -20–60°C for discharging; use the battery within the manual's environmental limits.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-pdp-temperature-desktop-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="SuntNeew Group 31 battery and RV shown in cold-weather operating conditions" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
<article class="story"><h2>Four practical charging paths—when each uses the right equipment.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>Plan LiFePO4-compatible CC/CV charge sources: an AC charger, solar with an MPPT controller, an alternator through a DC-to-DC charger, or a generator feeding a compatible charger. Do not connect sources directly to the battery terminals.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-amazon-aplus-charging-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Four LiFePO4-compatible charging paths for the SuntNeew Group 31 battery" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
<article class="story"><h2>Expand from one G31 to a planned 4S / 4P system.</h2><div class="story-copy"><p>Use matched batteries of the same model, capacity and state of charge. The listed architecture supports up to 4 in series or 4 in parallel, and up to 16 matched batteries in a 4P4S bank; follow the manual for balancing, protection and cabling.</p></div><img src="{{ 'sn-opt-suntneew-rv-g31-pdp-expansion-desktop-960.webp' | asset_url }}" alt="Matched SuntNeew Group 31 batteries arranged as an expandable off-grid battery bank" loading="lazy" width="960" height="644"></article>
</section>
