<section class="detail-section" role="tabpanel" tabindex="0" id="g31m-faq" aria-labelledby="g31m-tab-faq" hidden>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<details class="faq-item"><summary>What conditions apply to the cycle-life references?</summary><div><p>The approved G31 reference tiers are 4,000+ cycles at 100% depth of discharge, 6,000 cycles at 80% DoD and 15,000 cycles at 60% DoD. Actual cycle life varies with charge and discharge rate, temperature, maintenance, depth of discharge and operating conditions.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-item"><summary>Is Up to 10-Year Life the same as the 5-Year Limited Warranty?</summary><div><p>No. Up to 10-Year Life is a product-life reference under suitable use. The 5-Year Limited Warranty covers eligible defects under the model-specific warranty terms; it does not guarantee ten years of product life.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-item"><summary>What is included in 24/7 Support?</summary><div><p>You can contact SuntNeew support for product setup, charging, Bluetooth, installation and after-sales questions. Provide the order information, model number and photos or readings relevant to the issue.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-item"><summary>Can this battery be used to start an engine?</summary><div><p>No. This is a deep-cycle auxiliary battery and is not intended to start a vehicle, boat engine or other device. Do not use it as a starting battery.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-item"><summary>What should I confirm before installation?</summary><div><p>Confirm the 339 × 185 × 218mm enclosure, terminal position, hold-down, upright mounting, cable route and service clearance. Size conductors, fuses, disconnects, inverter and charging sources for the complete DC system.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-item"><summary>Are the appliance runtime figures guaranteed?</summary><div><p>No. They are theoretical estimates based on 1,280Wh rated energy and the stated appliance loads. Actual runtime changes with duty cycle, inverter efficiency, battery condition, temperature and the real power draw of the connected equipment.</p></div></details>
<details class="faq-item"><summary>Can an IP65 battery be submerged?</summary><div><p>No. IP65 means the enclosure is dust-tight and protected against water jets. It is not an immersion rating; keep the battery secured, upright and protected in accordance with the product manual.</p></div></details>
</section>
